  m_Name: RoomData-Ooty_AugmentedRealityApp
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  ProjectName: Augmented Reality App
  ClientName: Ooty
  Tags: 68
  Texts:
  - category: 0
    info: Lead Developer.
  - category: 1
    info: "Ooty is a trademark of the Black Oak Company (now K\u014Dz\u014Dwood Industries),
      which builds prefabricated and modular wooden structures: houses, bungalows,
      accommodation modules, and commercial and tourism buildings.\r\n\r\n"
  - category: 2
    info: 'An augmented reality app for Android and iOS that showcases the client''s
      product range. Users can:

      - Place houses at real size to walk around
      them, or scale them down for an overview,

      - View interiors,

      -
      Design their own house in a custom in-app house editor.'
  - category: 3
    info: The app had to run on both iOS and Android, which meant supporting two
      different AR frameworks, ARKit and ARCore, in a single Unity project.
  - category: 9
    info: '- Studied both SDKs in depth and identified the minimal set of components
      each one needed.

      - Integrated both into the same scene and adjusted
      them to coexist without conflicts.

      - Wrote a platform-detection layer
      that enables the right framework for iOS or Android.'
